From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:44:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 079/117] Revert "media: iris: Fix out-of-bounds read in
 timestamp metadata fallback"

Replaced by the list's v2 of the same fix (patchwork series 1213804), which
takes a different approach; the two must never be carried together.

This reverts commit 07761a95be09 (our pick of v1, media: iris: Fix out-of-bounds read in timestamp metadata fallback).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
index 67384e9480282..c32706a1ca30e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -865,11 +865,9 @@ static void iris_get_ts_metadata(struct iris_inst *inst, u64 timestamp_ns,
 		return;
 	}
 
-	i = inst->metadata_idx ? inst->metadata_idx - 1 : 0;
-
 	vbuf->flags &= ~mask;
-	vbuf->flags |= inst->tss[i].flags;
-	vbuf->timecode = inst->tss[i].tc;
+	vbuf->flags |= inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].flags;
+	vbuf->timecode = inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].tc;
 }
 
 int iris_vb2_buffer_done(struct iris_inst *inst, struct iris_buffer *buf)
-- 
2.43.0

